[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Jumbo Versus the Police]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.07]Why did the police have to push Jumbo off the main street? | 为什么警察不得不把“江宝”推离大街？
[00:17.78]Last Christmas, the circus owner, Jimmy Gates, decided to take some presents to a children's hospital. | 去年圣诞节，马戏团老板吉米·盖茨决定给一家儿童医院送些礼物。
[00:26.85]Dressed up as Father Christmas and accompanied by a 'guard of honour' of six pretty girls, | 他装扮成圣诞老人，由6个漂亮姑娘组成的“仪仗队”陪同，
[00:34.00]he set off down the main street of the city riding a baby elephant called Jumbo. | 骑上一头名叫“江宝”的小象，沿着城市的主要街道出发了。
[00:41.60]He should have known that the police would never allow this sort of thing. | 他本该知道警察绝不会允许这种事情发生。
[00:47.87]A policeman approached Jimmy and told him he ought to have gone along a side street as Jumbo was holding up the traffic. | 一个警察走近吉米，告诉他本该走小街，因为“江宝”阻碍了交通。
[00:57.78]Though Jimmy agreed to go at once, Jumbo refused to move. | 虽然吉米同意马上走，但“江宝”却拒绝挪动。
[01:04.87]Fifteen policemen had to push very hard to get him off the main street. | 15个警察不得不使劲推才把它推离大街。
[01:11.05]The police had a difficult time, but they were most amused. | 警察费了很大劲，但他们感到非常有趣。
[01:16.72]'Jumbo must weigh a few tons,' said a policeman afterwards, | “江宝一定有好几吨重，”事后一位警察说，
[01:22.77]'so it was fortunate that we didn't have to carry him. | “幸好我们不必把它抬走。
[01:27.79]Of course, we should arrest him, but as he has a good record, we shall let him off this time.' | 当然，我们应该逮捕它，但由于它表现一贯良好，这次我们饶了它。”
